---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Résumé | Sanduni G. Hewa" description="Résumé of Sanduni G. Hewa, a data engineer and analytics engineer specializing in Microsoft Fabric, Databricks, PySpark, SQL, and Power BI.">
  <main class="resume-page" id="main">
    <nav class="resume-nav" aria-label="Résumé navigation">
      <a href="/">← Back to portfolio</a>
      <button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save PDF</button>
    </nav>
    <header class="resume-header">
      <p>Data Engineer · Analytics Engineer · SQL Developer</p>
      <h1>Sanduni G. Hewa</h1>
      <div><span>Buford, GA</span><a href="mailto:sandurash19@gmail.com">sandurash19@gmail.com</a><a href="https://github.com/sanduni-hewa">GitHub</a><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/sanduni-galbokka-hewa">LinkedIn</a></div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Profile</h2>
      <p>Microsoft-certified data engineer with hands-on experience designing cloud-based analytical systems using Microsoft Fabric, Databricks, PySpark, SQL, Delta Lake, and Power BI. Builds scalable ETL/ELT pipelines, governed lakehouse models, data-quality controls, and performance-focused transformations that turn high-volume source data into reliable decision-ready products.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technical expertise</h2>
      <dl class="resume-skills">
        <div><dt>Data platforms</dt><dd>Microsoft Fabric, Databricks, Azure Data Factory, AWS S3, OneLake, Delta Lake</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Data engineering</dt><dd>Python, PySpark, Spark SQL, ETL/ELT, incremental ingestion, medallion architecture, orchestration, data quality</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Analytics engineering</dt><dd>T-SQL, dimensional modeling, star schemas, stored procedures, Power BI, DAX, Direct Lake, RLS</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Database engineering</dt><dd>PostgreSQL, SQL Server, relational schema design, CTEs, window functions, query optimization, RBAC</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <article class="resume-role">
        <div><h3>IT Developer · Mathnasium</h3><time>Sep 2025 — Present</time></div>
        <ul><li>Developed JavaScript and Playwright automation that reduced manual administrative effort by approximately 80%.</li><li>Designed a Python student-retention pipeline that automated Excel ingestion, segmented at-risk students, and triggered REST API notifications.</li><li>Implemented ingestion validation and quality checks that maintained 100% record accuracy and prevented downstream reporting errors.</li></ul>
      </article>
      <article class="resume-role">
        <div><h3>Backend Developer · Lindenwood University</h3><time>Jan — May 2025</time></div>
        <ul><li>Designed PostgreSQL schemas and optimized SQL transformations with CTEs and window functions, improving query performance by approximately 40% for real-time backend workflows.</li></ul>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Selected projects</h2>
      <article class="resume-project"><h3>FMCG Data Engineering Platform</h3><p>Built Databricks medallion pipelines that processed and standardized 90K+ transaction records using PySpark, Delta Lake, incremental ingestion, automated cleansing, deduplication, and star-schema modeling.</p></article>
      <article class="resume-project"><h3>NYC Taxi Analytics Engineering Platform</h3><p>Designed metadata-driven Microsoft Fabric pipelines for 13M+ records and replaced Dataflow Gen2 transformations with optimized SQL stored procedures, reducing presentation-layer processing from approximately three minutes to 30 seconds.</p></article>
      <article class="resume-project"><h3>Real-Time Transportation Data Pipeline</h3><p>Implemented Lakeflow Spark Declarative Pipelines with governed incremental ingestion for 356K+ records, reducing pipeline code from 135 to approximately 50 lines.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="resume-bottom">
      <div><h2>Education</h2><p><strong>B.S. Computer Science, Minor in Data Science</strong><br />Lindenwood University · GPA 3.9 · 2025</p></div>
      <div><h2>Certifications</h2><p>Microsoft Fabric Analytics Engineer Associate<br />Power BI Data Analyst Associate<br />Microsoft Azure Fundamentals</p></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .resume-page { max-width: 1050px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 30px 90px; }
  .resume-nav { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:80px; }
  .resume-nav a,.resume-nav button { border:0; background:none; color:var(--muted); font:11px var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; cursor:pointer; }
  .resume-header { padding-bottom:38px; border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink); }
  .resume-header > p { font:11px var(--font-mono); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; }
  .resume-header h1 { margin:8px 0 20px; font-size:clamp(48px,8vw,88px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.06em; }
  .resume-header div { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px 26px; font-size:13px; }
  .resume-page section { padding:34px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  .resume-page h2 { margin:0 0 20px; font:11px var(--font-mono); color:var(--cyan); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.12em; }
  .resume-page h3 { margin:0; font-size:19px; }
  .resume-page p,.resume-page li,.resume-page dd { color:var(--muted); }
  .resume-skills { margin:0; }
  .resume-skills div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:190px 1fr; gap:25px; padding:11px 0; }
  .resume-skills dt { font-weight:700; }
  .resume-skills dd { margin:0; }
  .resume-role { margin-bottom:28px; }
  .resume-role > div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:20px; }
  .resume-role time { font:11px var(--font-mono); }
  .resume-role ul { margin:12px 0 0; }
  .resume-project { margin-bottom:22px; }
  .resume-project p { margin:6px 0 0; }
  .resume-bottom { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:50px; border-bottom:0 !important; }
  @media(max-width:650px){.resume-skills div,.resume-bottom{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}.resume-role>div{display:block}.resume-nav{margin-bottom:50px}}
  @media print {.resume-nav{display:none}.resume-page{padding:0}.resume-page section{padding:20px 0}body{background:white;color:#07100d}.resume-page p,.resume-page li,.resume-page dd{color:#3e4c45}.resume-page h2{color:#52615a}}
</style>
